---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import Container from "@/components/container.astro";
import Subnav from "@/components/subnav.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "@/components/breadcrumbs.astro";
import { comparePages } from "@/data/navigation";
---

<Layout
  title="PgDesigner vs pgModeler — Feature Comparison"
  description="Detailed comparison of PgDesigner and pgModeler: features, pricing, git workflow, hazard detection, lint rules. Both are PostgreSQL-specialized — here's how they differ.">

  <Subnav items={comparePages} />

  <Container>
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto pt-16 pb-24">
      <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Compare", href: "/compare" }, { label: "vs pgModeler" }]} />
      <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-heading">
        PgDesigner vs pgModeler
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-body">pgModeler is the most established PostgreSQL visual modeler — 19 years of development, backed by Nullptr Labs. Since version 2.0 it ships in two editions: a free, open-source Community edition for modeling, and the paid Plus edition, which now holds database import, model diff and the SQL tools. Both tools are PG-specialized. Here's where they differ.</p>

      <div class="mt-12 prose max-w-none
        prose-headings:text-heading prose-headings:font-semibold
        prose-h2:text-2xl prose-h2:mt-12 prose-h2:mb-4
        prose-p:text-body prose-p:leading-relaxed
        prose-li:text-body
        prose-strong:text-heading
        prose-a:text-accent-text prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline
        prose-table:text-sm
        prose-th:text-heading prose-th:font-semibold prose-th:px-3 prose-th:pb-3
        prose-td:px-3 prose-td:py-2 prose-td:text-body
        prose-thead:border-border-default prose-tr:border-border-default">

        <h2>Feature comparison</h2>

        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Feature</th>
              <th style="text-align:center">PgDesigner</th>
              <th style="text-align:center">pgModeler</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>PostgreSQL version</td><td style="text-align:center">PG18 full spec</td><td style="text-align:center">PG18 initial (2.0, temporal keys)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>UI</td><td style="text-align:center">Browser-based</td><td style="text-align:center">Qt desktop</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Git-friendly diffs</td><td style="text-align:center">Yes (single-line XML)</td><td style="text-align:center">Plus only (split model, Git plugin)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Diff/ALTER engine</td><td style="text-align:center">Yes</td><td style="text-align:center">Plus only</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Hazard detection</td><td style="text-align:center">Yes (10 hazard codes)</td><td style="text-align:center">No</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Schema lint</td><td style="text-align:center">69 rules, 15 autofix</td><td style="text-align:center">Model validation and fix tool</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Sample data generator</td><td style="text-align:center">Yes (30+ heuristics)</td><td style="text-align:center">No</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Reverse engineering</td><td style="text-align:center">Yes (pg_catalog)</td><td style="text-align:center">Plus only</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Import PDD/DBS/DM2</td><td style="text-align:center">Yes</td><td style="text-align:center">No</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Views/functions diff</td><td style="text-align:center">Planned (Phase 2)</td><td style="text-align:center">Plus only</td></tr>
            <tr><td>SSH tunneling</td><td style="text-align:center">No</td><td style="text-align:center">Plus only</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Plugin system</td><td style="text-align:center">No</td><td style="text-align:center">Yes</td></tr>
            <tr><td>CLI</td><td style="text-align:center">Yes (single binary)</td><td style="text-align:center">Yes (requires Qt)</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2>Pricing</h2>

        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th></th>
              <th style="text-align:center">PgDesigner</th>
              <th style="text-align:center">pgModeler</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Individual</td><td style="text-align:center"><strong>Free</strong> (Apache-2.0)</td><td style="text-align:center">Plus: $65.90 / 6 months, $123.74 / 12 months (1 seat, 1 platform)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Team</td><td style="text-align:center"><strong>Free</strong></td><td style="text-align:center">Plus perpetual: $425.58 (2 seats, 1 platform)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Free tier</td><td style="text-align:center">Everything, Apache-2.0</td><td style="text-align:center">Community: modeling and SQL generation, build from source (GPLv3)</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Binaries</td><td style="text-align:center">GitHub Releases, Homebrew (public)</td><td style="text-align:center">Plus download only</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <h2>Where pgModeler is stronger</h2>

        <ul>
          <li><strong>Maturity</strong> — 19 years of development, battle-tested in production at scale</li>
          <li><strong>Views and functions diff</strong> — pgModeler Plus diffs views, functions, triggers. PgDesigner has this planned for Phase 2</li>
          <li><strong>Plugin system</strong> — custom extensions without modifying core code</li>
          <li><strong>SSH tunneling</strong> — connect to remote databases through SSH (Plus edition)</li>
          <li><strong>Database administration</strong> — built-in SQL execution and data browsing (Plus edition)</li>
          <li><strong>Large models</strong> — multi-scene canvases and attribute collapsing for big schemas</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Where PgDesigner is stronger</h2>

        <ul>
          <li><strong>Hazard detection</strong> — 10 hazard codes (DELETES_DATA, TABLE_REWRITE, TABLE_RECREATE, COLUMN_RECREATE, TYPE_RECREATE, BACKFILL_REQUIRED, ENUM_ADD_VALUE, UNNAMED_CONSTRAINT, DETACH_PARTITION, REATTACH_PARTITION) warn you before risky ALTER statements</li>
          <li><strong>69 lint rules with autofix</strong> — vs basic validation in pgModeler</li>
          <li><strong>Diff and import for free</strong> — in pgModeler 2.0, database import and model diff moved to the paid Plus edition. In PgDesigner they are part of the open-source build and the CLI</li>
          <li><strong>Git-friendly by default</strong> — single-line diffs in the free version. pgModeler's split model and Git plugin are Plus-only</li>
          <li><strong>Sample data generator</strong> — FK-aware, 30+ name heuristics, reproducible with seed</li>
          <li><strong>Import from 5 sources</strong> — MicroOLAP .pdd, DbSchema .dbs, Toad .dm2, SQL, live DB</li>
          <li><strong>Browser UI from a single binary</strong> — no Qt runtime; the same UI on macOS, Linux and Windows</li>
          <li><strong>Price</strong> — free and open source (Apache-2.0), signed binaries included, vs $65.90 per 6 months for pgModeler Plus</li>
          <li><strong>Zero-dependency binary</strong> — single static binary vs Qt dependency chain</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Honest assessment</h2>

        <p>pgModeler is the more mature tool. If you need views/functions diff, SSH tunneling, or a plugin system today — pgModeler Plus is the better choice. PgDesigner's strengths are in the DBA-focused workflow: hazard detection, deep linting, sample data generation, and a git-native format. If your team reviews schema changes in PRs, PgDesigner fits that workflow better.</p>

      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-border-default">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-heading mb-3">Related</p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
          <a href="/features/diff" class="text-sm text-accent-text hover:underline">Diff & ALTER →</a>
          <a href="/features/lint" class="text-sm text-accent-text hover:underline">Schema Linter →</a>
          <a href="/pricing" class="text-sm text-accent-text hover:underline">Pricing →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16 flex gap-4">
        <a href="/docs/download" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg bg-blue-600 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-blue-500 transition-colors">
          Download PgDesigner
        </a>
        <a href="/features" class="inline-flex items-center rounded-lg border border-border-default px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-body hover:bg-surface-alt/50 transition-colors">
          View All Features
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Container>
</Layout>
